# Known legitimate domains (each including subdomains): only the initial fill of a new
# Host. agentbox setup installs it, agentbox migrate-lists takes it over once into
# /etc/agentbox/legitimate.json; after that only agentbox legitimate-add/-remove
# change it, changes here no longer reach the Host.
#
# Effect (proxy/agentbox-suspicious):
# - no pattern Signals (lookalike, tld, random-label, ...) for these domains, except
#   the blockchain pattern (rpc., mainnet, infura, ...): that stays a strong Signal;
# - hits of the HaGeZi lists for one of them or a subdomain do not count, so that
#   a faulty list does not disturb normal work; but not for the
#   builtin user-content domains (marked below): hits on their subdomains
#   count, anyone can publish there.
# The manual Watchlist (suspicious-domains) applies regardless. This list releases
# nothing; only the Allowlist does that.
#
# Only domains whose operator controls them itself. No hosts for arbitrary
# user content (amazonaws.com, pages.dev, vercel.app, jsdelivr.net, ...): real
# threats live there, which the lists know.

# GitHub and other code hosts; githubusercontent.com and github.io are builtin
# user-content domains, so their subdomains count like hosts for user content
